CHANGE.log
==========

Running log of fixes to the pythonic AviaNZ port (branch pyavianz), newest first.
Longer-form history: Changelog.md (AviaNZ) and hpc/CHANGES.md (avianz_hpc port).


2026-11-05  commits 3a96c3be, 6383739c, ca330b81, 9316b02f
-----------------------------------------------------------

PACKAGING / IMPORTS (3a96c3be)

* AviaNZ now imports itself one way only: absolute `avianz.src...` / `avianz.ext...`.
  ~100 bare `from src...` / `from ext import` lines in 22 files were rewritten.
  Before, running as a script could load the same module twice (`src.core.x` and
  `avianz.src.core.x`), each with its own state.
* pyproject.toml: package discovery searches from the repo root and installs only
  `avianz` (previously `where = ["avianz"]` installed `src`, `Config`, `Filters`,
  `hooks`, `ext` as separate top-level packages and not `avianz` itself). Added
  package-data for Config/, Filters/, ext/*.pyd|*.so, src/data/, src/resources/.
  Requires setuptools >= 64.
* `avianz` console command now points to `avianz.AviaNZ:main`. The launch code in
  AviaNZ.py is wrapped in `main()` and guarded by `if __name__ == "__main__"`, so
  importing the module no longer launches AviaNZ.
* New avianz/__main__.py: `python -m avianz [options]` (same options as `avianz`).
* avianz/__init__.py no longer imports Config, Docs, ext, Filters, hooks, src.
* Added empty __init__.py to src/ui/colourMaps, components, dialogs,
  dialogs_training, so a regular (non-editable) `pip install .` includes the GUI.
* Running `python avianz/AviaNZ.py` directly now needs the package installed
  (`pip install -e .`); use `avianz ...` or `python -m avianz ...` instead.

AviaNZ.py (3a96c3be)

* `-r` is a tuple since it accepts multiple recognisers: training (`-t`) and
  testing (`-u`) now take exactly one `-r` and pass the name, not the tuple
  (both were always failing validation).
* Batch mode with no `-r` reports the error again (`all()` of an empty tuple was True).
* Config is reloaded after the default is restored, fixing a NameError in GUI mode
  on first run or with a corrupt AviaNZconfig.txt.
* Bundled Filters/ may use subfolders; files are copied flat into the user's
  Filters folder (where filters(), NN model/ROC lookups and the Filter Manager look).
  Same file name in two subfolders: first in sorted order wins, with a warning.
  `__pycache__` and `Filters/__init__.py` are skipped.

MODEL LOADING

* 6383739c  src/models/model_loader.py: full-model .pth files pickled under the old
  module path `src.models.tf_to_torch_converter` (Kiwi (Nth Is Brown), Kiwi (Great
  Spotted), Kiwi (Little Spotted)_21-13-34) load again; the unpickler maps `src.*`
  to `avianz.src.*`. Symptom fixed: "Error loading model ...: No module named 'src'",
  "Loaded NN models: []".
* ca330b81  src/models/tf_to_torch_converter.py: `h5py` is imported only when
  converting a TensorFlow .h5 model, so loading a .pth needs no h5py. h5py is still
  needed for recognisers without a .pth (Bittern, Kiwi (Tokoeka Fiordland),
  Morepork, NZ Bats_NP).

CPU THREADS (9316b02f)

* src/models/gpu_config.py: new `available_cpu_count()` = OMP_NUM_THREADS if set,
  else CPUs in the process affinity mask (Slurm allocation), else os.cpu_count().
  `configure_cpu_threads()` and inference.generate_features_threaded() use it
  instead of os.cpu_count().
  Symptom fixed on Rāpoi AMD nodes (256 cores): "DEBUG: torch cpu thread count set
  to 256" then "DefaultCPUAllocator: can't allocate memory ... Error code 12" at
  the first NN segment, with MaxRSS only ~275 MB. On Rāpoi `--mem` also sets
  `ulimit -v`, and 256 threads' reserved memory exceeded it.

HPC (3a96c3be)

* hpc/solar/solar_survey.py runs `python -m avianz ...` with only the repo root on
  PYTHONPATH (was `python AviaNZ.py` with repo root + avianz/).
* hpc/avianz_hpc/_avianz.py and hpc/recogniser/train_recogniser.py add only the
  repo root to sys.path.
* hpc/avianz_hpc/core/model_trainer.py: `from models import GradientReversalLayer`
  -> `from avianz_hpc.core.models import ...` (DANN with AST would have crashed).

DOCS (3a96c3be)

* README.md: CLI examples use `avianz ...` / `python -m avianz ...`.

KNOWN ISSUES / NOT YET DONE

* `-s` / `-z` (cheatsheet, Zooniverse) crash: `avianz.src.ui.AviaNZ_manual_GUI` does
  not exist; `manual_interface.ManualInterface` takes the same arguments.
* Icon path `AviaNZ.ico` vs file `Avianz.ico` (fails on case-sensitive file systems).
* Missing files: Filters/NZ Bats.json (NZ Bats NN cannot load), and
  src/resources/images/volume-mute.png.
* `torch` and `spectrum` are used but not listed in pyproject.toml / requirements.txt.
* avianz/build_executable.py (upstream cx_Freeze script) cannot build this code.
* ext/ Cython modules are committed only as Windows/Python 3.10 builds; on Rāpoi build
  them in the job's venv: `cd ~/avianz/avianz/ext && python setup.py build_ext -i`
  (on a `parallel` compute node). Not yet in the HPC docs.
* Default Config/AviaNZconfig.txt has "previousMode": 1, so a fresh install skips
  the start screen.
* A single failed file stops a whole batch run ("Analysis failed") instead of being
  skipped.
* Rāpoi jobs: also set OMP_NUM_THREADS / MKL_NUM_THREADS / OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS /
  NUMBA_NUM_THREADS to the CPUs requested and MALLOC_ARENA_MAX=2 (e.g. in
  ~/avianz_env.sh); not yet in hpc/ docs or sbatch scripts.
